course: dictionary
lesson: 1227
title: One word, two machines and people
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: A bulldozer is a big, powerful machine with a wide metal blade at the front. It pushes earth, rocks and rubble out of the way. «A bulldozer pushes earth and rubble with a big blade at the front» tells you exactly what the machine does, so you can picture it.
explain: Read the whole sentence for more clues. Its caterpillar tracks grip the ground, so the machine can push over rough, muddy land without slipping. The sentence also says tracks were used on farm tractors before tanks, which is a little bit of history.
explain: The word also has an informal meaning: a bulldozer can be a person who forces their way and does not listen to others. Context helps you choose. If the sentence is about a machine, it means the machine. If it is about how someone behaves, it means the person. To bulldoze means to knock down or push through.
explain: Writers often use a word from one thing to describe another. «A glacier is a giant bulldozer and file» compares a glacier to a machine. Rocks frozen into the glacier scrape the land, just as a bulldozer pushes earth. Ask yourself: what is the same about these two things?
fact: A bulldozer is a big, powerful machine with a wide metal blade at the front.
fact: The informal meaning: a bulldozer is a person who forces their way and does not listen to others.
fact: To bulldoze means to knock down or push through.
fact: «Bulldozer» can describe a glacier as well, because a glacier also pushes and scrapes rock.
fact: Always check the context: a machine on a building site and a bossy person in a meeting are different meanings of the same word.
exercise: «A bulldozer pushes earth and rubble with a big blade at the front.» What does the bulldozer use to push? | A rope tied to a tree | *A wide metal blade at the front | Long wings that flap | A hose full of water
exercise: Ben says a classmate who never listens and shoves his idea through is a bulldozer. What does bulldozer mean here? | A kind teacher who asks everyone's opinion | *A person who forces their way and does not listen | A big yellow machine on a building site | A small garden bird
exercise: «A glacier is a giant bulldozer and file.» Why is a glacier called a bulldozer? | *It pushes and scrapes rock along, like a machine pushing earth | It is a type of cloud | It is made of wood and has wheels | It only melts in summer
test: «The old house was bulldozed to make room for a new road.» What happened to the house? | It was given a new roof | *It was knocked down | It was painted bright blue | It was moved to the seaside
test: What does the verb «to bulldoze» mean? | *To knock down or push through | To count coins carefully | To drive slowly around a park | To sing loudly in assembly
exam: Why do safety rules tell children to stay away from building sites and big machines? | Because bulldozers only work at night | *Because drivers cannot always see them | Because the machines are too small to notice | Because children must help carry the rubble
